{"verdict": "accept", "reason": "`ansible.builtin.user` with `password_lock: yes` runs `usermod -L` on Linux, which prefixes the stored hash with '!' and so disables password authentication for 'service'. Baseline: the unlocked hash becomes locked. Adversarial: the hash already starts with '!', so the module reports no change and the password stays disabled. No other account settings are altered. One caveat: `become: true` wraps tasks in sudo even when already root, so this assumes sudo is present in the container."}
```

